  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Strengthening Public Sector Management Program, Subprogram 1</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The proposed program supports improved governance and accountability across the public sector in Papua New Guinea by improving fiscal management, enhancing state-owned enterprise (SOE) governance, and strengthening accountability institutions through three mutually reinforcing reform areas. The program will be financed through two policy-based loans of $100 million for subprogram 1 in 2024 and, indicatively, $150 million for subprogram 2 in 2026. The program builds on and expands the scope of reforms supported through previous Asian Development Bank (ADB) policy-based lending (PBL).</narrative>
  </description>
