   <indicator measure="5">
    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">1.1. To improve domestic resource mobilization and create space for essential development spending, (i) NEC adopted the Medium-term Revenue Strategy 2023&#x2013;2027 (MTRS) in October 2023 that encompasses all main revenue collecting agencies and taxes and identifies legal, regulatory and institutional reforms needed to improve revenue collections; (ii) the Non-tax Revenue Act 2022 was gazetted on 21 April 2023, which will centralize statutory bodies&#x2019; revenues into the Consolidated Revenue Fund to improve governance and accountability in the management of non-tax revenues; and (iii) the Treasurer approved NTRA determination agreements for 13 (out of 24) statutory authorities that collect non-tax revenue as part of a phased arrangement to implement the NTRA Act.</narrative>
    </title>
   </indicator>
   <indicator measure="5">
    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">1.2. To enhance macro-fiscal stability through enhanced debt management, the DoT operationalized a new fit-for-purpose debt management system, and completed the migration of debt data, including information on government guarantees.</narrative>
    </title>
   </indicator>
   <indicator measure="5">
    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">1.3. To enhance climate resilience of land transport network in PNG, DOWH adopted a prioritized plan to implement the department&#x2019;s Climate Change Policy.</narrative>
    </title>
   </indicator>
